{
    "sheet":  "adaptation",
    "notes":  "One row per Noita damage type. message_key is the damage message Noita sends to damage_received; field is the DamageModelComponent damage_multipliers field (\u0027drowning\u0027 has none: it works through air_needed / air_lack_of_damage instead). Boss: after taking boss_threshold_frac of max HP of a type (x boss_threshold_growth per earlier adaptation, each hit counted x boss_progress_mult) the wheel turns and that type is set to boss_result_mult. Player perk: every player_hits_per_step hits of a type (at most one hit counted per player_hit_cooldown_frames) multiply it by player_step_mult; the player_max_steps-th step makes the player fully immune (drowning: no air needed). Fire burns in rapid ticks, so it counts slower on both. aliases: other damage messages that count as this type (most curse sources name themselves, e.g. the sun or the cursed rock). material: contact with harmful materials (lava, acid, toxic gas, cursed rock...), recognised by the frame the game last dealt material damage; immunity turns materials_damage off; the player\u0027s steps scale materials_how_much_damage.",
